\ctlchange sends a MIDI Control Change message.
It takes four integer arguments, the MIDI port, the
channel, the controller number, and the value:

\ctlchange 1 1 7 100

The line above sends value 100 to controller 7 (volume)
on channel 1 of MIDI port 1.

The port must already be open, with \openmidiport or with
the midiport method of an instrument, otherwise you will
get a "selected MIDI port is not open" error.
The channel must be between 1 and 16, and the value
between 0 and 127.
